How the Fish Audio Materials were modified:
- Routed experts were pruned per layer using speech-calibrated routing statistics. Layers 0, 1, 2
  and 36 keep all 256 experts; every other layer keeps 100 of 256 (4,640 of 10,240 expert slots).
  Routers were cut to the kept rows.
- The kept experts were quantized to IQ3_XXS using an importance matrix from speech calibration
  data. The dense backbone (attention / Gated DeltaNet), the embeddings and the multi-token audio
  tower were quantized to Q8_0. The codec weights are unchanged (F16).
- The output head was reduced to the EOS row plus the 4,096 semantic-token rows (speech only).
- Routers and shared experts were refit layer by layer against the original model's activations.
- The result was distilled from the original model for 100 optimizer steps on Japanese and English
  speech (knowledge distillation on the semantic and audio-tower distributions). Rank-64 LoRA
  updates of the attention and Gated DeltaNet projections were merged into the weights; routers,
  shared experts, norms and the speech head were updated directly.
- The package is a GGUF for audio.cpp and requires the included drama3-small audio.cpp patch.
